# Cppcheck suppressions. MISRA C:2012 is enforced strictly: every MISRA entry
# below is a documented deviation (see docs/MISRA_DEVIATIONS.md). Prefer an
# inline "// cppcheck-suppress <id> ; Deviation Dn: ..." comment at the site;
# use this file only where cppcheck ignores inline comments.

# External code - Pico SDK, FreeRTOS and TinyUSB sources and headers (Deviation D0)
*:*lib/*
# Pico SDK headers generated into the build tree (e.g. pico/version.h) (Deviation D0)
*:*/generated/*

# Rule 2.5 (Deviation D7): the addon cannot track macro use across translation
# units and reports macros used only in .c files, plus FreeRTOS/TinyUSB
# configuration macros consumed by lib/ code.
misra-c2012-2.5:*

# Rule 8.7 (Deviation D2): callbacks and hooks with external linkage that are
# referenced only by lib/ code. Cross-translation-unit findings ignore inline
# suppressions, so scripts/run_cppcheck.sh suppresses the line that follows each
# "MISRA Deviation D2 (Rule 8.7)" comment.
